---
/**
 * The privacy page.
 *
 * ⚠️ This page says the site collects nothing. That is only true while there
 * is no analytics script, no ads, no embedded video, no web fonts served from
 * somewhere that logs, and no sign-up form. If any of those is ever added,
 * REWRITE THIS PAGE IN THE SAME CHANGE — and note that ads or analytics also
 * bring cookie consent for visitors in the UK and EU, and disclosure duties in
 * California.
 *
 * Search traffic is measured with Google Search Console, which is verified by
 * a DNS record and puts nothing on the page. That is why this promise can
 * stay true and still leave the site measurable.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/content.mjs";

const updated = "September 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${SITE.domain} handles your data: no accounts, no tracking, no analytics. Your practice progress stays in your own browser.`}
  breadcrumb={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy", href: "/privacy" },
  ]}
>
  <main id="main">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      Last updated {updated}. The short version: nothing about you leaves your
      browser.
    </p>

    <section class="card legal">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>Nothing about you.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          There is no account and no sign-up. You are never asked for your name
          or your email.
        </li>
        <li>There are no ads, no analytics scripts and no tracking cookies.</li>
        <li>
          Your answers, scores and progress are saved in your own browser and
          never sent anywhere. We cannot see them.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="card legal">
      <h2>Where your progress lives</h2>
      <p>
        In your browser's own storage, on the device you study on. That has two
        consequences worth knowing:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          It stays on that one device and that one browser. Studying on your
          phone won't show up on your laptop.
        </li>
        <li>
          Clearing your browsing data, or studying in a private window, erases
          it. There is no backup and no way to recover it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That's fine for a few weeks of study, which is what most people need
        this for — but it's better to know it up front than to discover it the
        week of your test.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card legal">
      <h2>What the server sees</h2>
      <p>
        The same thing every web server sees when you open any page: the request
        itself. The site is static files on a content delivery network, so there
        is no database, no profile and nothing tied to you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card legal">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>See also: <a href="/terms">terms of use</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
